Declare jq.bzl's toolchain hub repo reproducible so it can use the repo contents cache.

Upstream marked `jq_platform_repo` reproducible in
https://github.com/bazel-contrib/jq.bzl/pull/70 but stopped short of
`jq_toolchains_repo`, which only writes a generated BUILD file derived from its own
attributes and is therefore trivially reproducible. Without this, `jq_toolchains`
misses the remote repo contents cache on every CI runner.

Not yet raised upstream.

--- a/jq/toolchain/toolchain.bzl
+++ b/jq/toolchain/toolchain.bzl
@@ -106,6 +106,12 @@
     # Base BUILD file for this repository
     rctx.file("BUILD.bazel", build_content)
 
+    # Bazel <8.3.0 lacks rctx.repo_metadata
+    if not hasattr(rctx, "repo_metadata"):
+        return None
+
+    return rctx.repo_metadata(reproducible = True)
+
 jq_toolchains_repo = repository_rule(
     _jq_toolchains_repo_impl,
     doc = """Creates a repository with toolchain definitions for all known platforms
